 "notes": [
  "The product video's shortest length is 'About 30 s': a 20 s video cannot be asked for; the steps it makes have to be shortened by hand afterwards.",
  "Explode moves the pieces at once and cannot be tried again with another distance: a second Explode moves them further from where they now are (it explodes the exploded state). The user must press Everything back to CAD position (in 4 Motion's main panel, above) first \u2013 a different fold.",
  "To hold the exploded view the user works out the gap between the two steps' times by hand (pose ends 7 s, back starts 12 s); nothing shows the steps on a time line, so the 'hold' is invisible.",
  "Go to pose moves every piece at once along a straight line; for one-after-another the user needs the other step kind (Assembly sequence), which has its own exploded places (not the pose) \u2013 two ways to explode with different settings, nothing links them.",
  "Put together has to be told the same subassembly again (Use selected), and its own Direction / Order: nothing copies them from the Take apart step. A 'Take apart, hold, put back' preset would be 1 step."
